WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:09.252
Catering, private dining, interviews, site visits. Connect your company calendars, and see what’s coming up, how much is booked, and when you’re busiest.

2
00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:18.333
In the Admin console, open Apps. Google Calendar and Microsoft Calendar have their own group, Calendars. Connect one, or both.

3
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:26.395
Sign in with the account whose calendars you want, and approve read-only access. Worklynq never creates or changes events.

4
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:35.111
Then choose the calendars that count. The main one is ticked. Add shared ones, like Catering and events, and leave out ones like public holidays.

5
00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:40.409
A meeting on more than one calendar, or in both Google and Microsoft, counts once.

6
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.485
On a dashboard, Coming up lists today’s and the next seven days’ bookings, soonest first.

7
00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:54.251
Count meetings, or hours booked, by calendar, organizer, day of the week, or hour of the day, to see your busiest times.

8
00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:02.913
To add one, click Add widget and just ask, like: meetings this week by calendar. Calendar widgets start out for System Admins only.

